# Review and Audit Roles

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `specs/README.md`. Choose a reviewer for a specific uncertainty or risk; do not route every task through all reviewers.

| Need | Canonical prompt | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Engineering or architecture correctness | `agents/roles/solution-reviewer-agent.md` | approve / revise / reject |
| Significant permissions, invitations, realtime, migrations or other sensitive boundaries | `agents/roles/security-reliability-agent.md` | pass / pass-with-notes / block; independent review required |
| Doubtful task/spec completeness | `agents/roles/prompt-task-auditor-agent.md` | ready / needs-clarification |
| Complex or doubtful test coverage | `agents/roles/test-reviewer-agent.md` | coverage-sufficient / coverage-incomplete |
| Complex or uncertain interaction design | `agents/roles/ux-critic-agent.md` | ux-approved / ux-issues-found |

Review against the current feature contract and its R/AC identifiers. Derive permissions and lifecycle rules from it rather than imposing owner-only controls, expiry rules, timing targets, or new infrastructure. Check test-first practice and verification in proportion to executable behavior; documentation/planning without runtime changes does not require application tests.

Findings need concrete evidence, affected requirement/file, impact, and a necessary correction. A blocking security/reliability finding prevents acceptance until fixed and rechecked. Return concise readable findings; use a machine schema only for a named actual consumer.
